PROPOSAL — patch for a code owner to apply to .github/workflows/ci.yml
(the workflow layer is frozen and CODEOWNER-gated; see README.md in this
directory).

What it does: extends the `code` negation filter in ci.yml's `changes` job
so the docs-site toolchain files (package.json, package-lock.json, .nvmrc)
and the attribution file (NOTICE) no longer count as "code" — a PR touching
only those paths skips the Rust lanes and is gated by the docs-site lane
instead — and widens `!LICENSE` to `!LICENSE*` so any future license-file
variants are covered too.

Apply from the repo root (verify first):

    git apply --check docs/internal/proposals/ci-yml-docs-filter.patch
    git apply docs/internal/proposals/ci-yml-docs-filter.patch

--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -56,7 +56,11 @@
                         - "!*.md"
                         - "!**/*.md"
                         - "!docs/**"
-                        - "!LICENSE"
+                        - "!LICENSE*"
+                        - "!NOTICE"
+                        - "!package.json"
+                        - "!package-lock.json"
+                        - "!.nvmrc"
 
     fmt:
         needs: [changes]
